# Pantos Smart Contract Audit Report

## Overview

This folder contains a public smart contract audit report for **Pantos**, the multichain interoperability project created by the team behind **Bitpanda**.

Softstack audited the **Pantos Core** smart contract infrastructure, providing security review support for a project focused on cross-blockchain token transfers and multichain asset interoperability.

## About Pantos

**Pantos** is a multichain token and interoperability project initiated by the Bitpanda team. It is designed to make digital assets more portable across blockchains and to support a more connected multichain ecosystem.

That makes Pantos much more than a simple token project. It is infrastructure aimed at solving one of the most important technical problems in Web3: how assets and token systems can move securely across different blockchain environments.

## Why This Project Matters

Pantos is an important public reference because it is tied directly to the broader **Bitpanda** ecosystem and its long-term infrastructure vision around multichain interoperability.

This audit is especially relevant as a public proof point for:

- multichain smart contract security
- interoperability infrastructure audits
- Bitpanda blockchain infrastructure
- core protocol smart contract reviews
- security work for cross-chain asset systems

For buyers and partners, this is strong social proof because it shows Softstack supporting security-critical blockchain infrastructure connected to one of Europe's best-known digital asset platforms.

## Softstack Audit Scope

This folder contains the following public report:

- [Softstack_Smart_Contract_Audit_Pantos_Core_21102024.pdf](./Softstack_Smart_Contract_Audit_Pantos_Core_21102024.pdf)

The file name indicates a **core smart contract audit**, which makes this a particularly strong proof point for foundational protocol security rather than a peripheral feature review.

